      "math_academy_id": "q-141253",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "If $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are polynomials of degree $3$ and $5$, respectively, what is the degree of $P\\cdot Q?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $P$ is a polynomial of degree $3,$ the leading term contains an ${x}^{3}.$\n\nSince $Q$ is a polynomial of degree $5,$ the leading term contains an ${x}^{5}.$\n\nIn $P\\cdot Q,$ the ${x}^{3}$ term in $P$ multiplies with the ${x}^{5}$ term in $Q$ to form a term containing ${x}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{5}={x}^{3+5}={x}^{8}.$\n\nTherefore, the degree of $P\\cdot Q$ must be $8.$",
